1##emote pulls a wrinkled piece of paper from his vest.
1##say This is a little something I found the other day..
2##say I thought it was kinda nifty..
1##ahem
2##say Below the thunders of the upper deep,
2##say Far, far beneath in the abysmal sea,
2##say His ancient, dreamless, uninvaded sleep
2##say The Kraken sleepeth: faintest sunlights flee
2##say About his shadowy sides; above him sell
2##say Huge sponges of millennial growth and height;
2##say And far away into the sickly light,
2##say From many a wondrous grot and secret cell
2##say Unnumber'd and enormous polypi
2##say Winnow with giant arms the slumbering green.
2##say There hath he lain for ages, and will lie
2##say Battening upon huge sea-worms in his sleep,
2##say Until the latter fire shall heat the deep;
2##say Then once by man and anges to be seen,
2##say In roaring he shall rise and on the surface die.
1##grin sheepishly
1##say That's it.
2##bow
1##@stop_poem
1##END
